1. Project Overview
Project Name: Digital Impact Hub Current Version: 30.0 (Personal Operating System Edition) Goal: To provide a comprehensive, "Local-First" Single-Page Application (SPA) for a Digital Pedagogy Coach. The tool manages tasks, projects, strategy, meeting notes, and reporting, functioning as a personal operating system without requiring IT server infrastructure. Core Philosophy:

Zero-Infrastructure: Runs entirely in a browser as a single HTML file.

Local-First: Data is stored in a local JSON file (digital-coach-data.json) via the File System Access API.

Governance-Ready: Built to align daily tasks with high-level strategic KPIs and Quality Assurance mechanisms.

2. Technical Architecture
Stack: HTML5, Tailwind CSS (CDN), Alpine.js (CDN), Chart.js (CDN), Canvas Confetti (CDN).

Data Model: Single JSON object containing:

projects: Array of project objects (Tasks, Updates, Meetings, KPIs).

todos: Array of "Hopper" tasks (Action items).

meetingNotes: Array of notebook entries (Linked to projects/strategy).

calendarEvents: Array of scheduled blocks/meetings.

settings: Configuration for Priorities (Pillars), KPIs, Meeting Categories, QA Sources.

Key Logic:

appData(): The central Alpine.js component managing state.

Reactivity: Updates to arrays (like projects) use spread syntax ([...array]) or reassignment to ensure UI reactivity.

Persistence: window.showOpenFilePicker handles the read/write connection to the local JSON file.

3. Strategic Framework (The "Why")
The project is structured around 4 Strategic Pillars (consolidated from an initial 7):

Digital Ecosystem & Standards: (Infrastructure, Teams Health Checks, Equipment Audits).

Pedagogy, Assessment & Innovation: (AI, Visualisers, Digital Inking, Autonomous Learning).

Inclusion & Accessibility: (Assistive Tech, Accessibility Toolkit, SEND support).

Capacity Building & Quality Assurance: (Digital Champions, TLA Upskilling, Learning Walks).

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs):

Teaching Quality Indicators, QIP Traction, Staff Capability, Staff Confidence, Student Experience, Retention Proxy, Value for Money, Digital Champions.

4. Current Functionality (The "What")
Planner: A Kanban-style "Hopper" for tasks vs. a Weekly Calendar for time-blocking.

Dashboard: High-level view of Active Projects, Actions Due, and QIP Traction. Toggle between "Strategy" and "Governance" views.

Projects: Deep management of initiatives with "Micro-Tasks," "Evidence Locker," and "Governance Tags" (KPIs, QA Links).

Meeting Hub: A 3-pane notebook system for categorizing notes (1:1s, HoAs, etc.) and linking them to projects. Includes "Quick Actions" to fire tasks to the Planner.

Timeline (Gantt): Dynamic visual roadmap with "Year/Quarter/Month" zoom levels and "Swimlane" filtering by Strategy or Stand-alone.

Reports: "Deep Dive" analytics allowing drill-down by Dept, Staff, or KPI.

5. Known Issues / Roadmap
File Permissions: The browser requires the user to re-grant permission to the file on every page reload (Security feature of the API).

Mobile Experience: Optimized for Desktop/Tablet; mobile layout is functional but could be refined.

Future Dev: Potential to add "Recurring Tasks" or "Template Projects" for repeated workflows.

